Bucketed Grouping + Fill Capacity Fix (v2.8.11)
Bug 1 — Flat section assignment (api.php)

When a section had values=["Nolan","Spielberg"], all matching items were gathered into a single flat list and globally sorted. Now the loop iterates each value individually, building a separate contiguous sub-group per value (in the order the user specified). Each item gets a bucket_label field. Single-value or empty-values sections behave as before.

Bug 2 — $unplaced always returned 0 (api.php)

The old formula ($placedTop + $totalBottom) > $totalCapacity was always false because $placedTop counted placed items (already capped by capacity), never exceeding $totalCapacity. Fixed to:

$unplaced = max(0, ($totalTopRemainder - $placedTop) + ($totalBottom - $placedBottom));

Where $totalTopRemainder = all items attempted, and $placedBottom is now tracked in the bottom fill loop.

Bug 3 — No bucket headers in preview (app.js)

_renderWizardPreview now detects when bucket_label changes across items on the same shelf and inserts a purple chip label (e.g. Nolan) with a │ visual separator before the first item of each new bucket.


