v2.8.13 pushed. Here's exactly what was fixed:

Goal A — Correct Physical Inventory Source
Bug 1 (root cause of box sets never appearing): include_boxsets and include_wishlist were always false. The frontend puts them inside recipe.remainder.include_boxsets, but the backend was reading $input['include_boxsets'] (top-level). Fixed with a priority chain: $recipe['remainder']['include_boxsets'] ?? $input['options']['include_boxsets'] ?? $input['include_boxsets'] ?? false.

Bug 2 (double-placement prevention): Copies that are physically inside a container are now unconditionally filtered from $allCopies. A new query reads all container_contents.copy_id for the user and removes those from the pool. This applies whether box sets are included or excluded — you can't place both the box set AND its individual discs.

Container query now returns contained_count (via LEFT JOIN container_contents), so box-set items carry their disc count.

Empty-pool guard relaxed: fails only when both $allCopies AND $allContainers are empty, so a user with only box sets and include_boxsets=true can still plan.

All items now carry: movie_id, year, rating, item_type (single|boxset), enabling correct sort-by-year/rating and future consumer use.

Goal B — Named Blocks for Flat Sections
New $getPrimaryValue helper extracts the first director/studio/genre/cert from enriched metadata (falls back to movies table string fields). Flat sections (values=[]) now set bucket_label from this helper and sort bucket-first (contiguous groups per value), then by the section's secondary sort. Result: "Director: Christopher Nolan" and "Director: Steven Spielberg" blocks appear instead of "Director: Other".

Box-set items carry bucket_label: 'Box Sets' — they form a distinct "Box Sets" block in the preview.


