What was wrong and what's fixed
Root Cause 1 — Stale cache silenced get_layout_sections
// OLD — skipped profile re-fetch if ANY profiles were already loaded
if (layoutProfiles.length === 0) {
    await loadLayoutProfiles();
}
const activeLayout = layoutProfiles.find(l => l.is_active == 1);
if (activeLayout) { /* fetch sections */ }

If the user visited Shelf View before the wizard ran (or the first load returned no active layout), layoutProfiles was populated with all is_active=0 entries. On every subsequent visit the guard length === 0 was false, the re-fetch was skipped, .find(is_active==1) returned undefined, and get_layout_sections was never called.

Root Cause 2 — refreshAllShelfViews only refreshed sections on the shelf-view tab
After saving a wizard plan from any other tab, _layoutSections stayed []. Sections only appeared if the user happened to be on the shelf-view tab at save time.

Fix — loadActiveLayoutSections() (new helper)
async function loadActiveLayoutSections() {
    try { await loadLayoutProfiles(); } catch(e) {}   // always fresh
    const activeLayout = layoutProfiles.find(l => l.is_active == 1);
    if (activeLayout) {
        const sections = await apiCall('get_layout_sections', { layout_id: activeLayout.id });
        _layoutSections = sections || [];
    } else { _layoutSections = []; }
}

loadShelfViewBrowse() — calls loadActiveLayoutSections() unconditionally (no cache gate)
